<title>UK: UK net consumer credit up 1.22 bln stg in Feb.</title>
<headline>UK net consumer credit up 1.22 bln stg in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the following seasonally adjusted consumer credit data -</p>
<p>NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in MLN STG)</p>
<p>					     Feb     Jan		Feb,96</p>
<p> Total net lending		     3,054   2,741 (2,767)  2,040</p>
<p>  -- Consumer credit		   1,221   844   (853)    652</p>
<p>  -- Secured on dwellings	    1,833   1,897 (1,914)  1,389</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN of net consumer lending BY SOURCE -</p>
<p>  -- Banks				 994    634    (631)    516</p>
<p>  -- Building societies		 31     27    (28)     26</p>
<p>  -- Other specialist lenders	198     183   (n/a)    94</p>
<p>  -- Retailers			     4	 4   (10)     14</p>
<p>  -- Insurance companies		-6	-4   (-4)	2</p>
<p> Credit Card			     337     89     (88)    121</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted, in PCT)</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	     1.6     1.1  (1.2)	1.0</p>
<p>		  annualised 3mth     17.9    17.0  (7.2)     14.2</p>
<p>    &quot;	 &quot;		yr/yr    17.5    16.8  (6.7)     13.1</p>
<p>Total personal borrowing mth/mth     0.6   0.6  (0.6)    0.4</p>
<p>		    annualised 3mth	7.2   7.1  (7.2)    5.6</p>
<p>    &quot;	 &quot;	  &quot;     yr/yr     6.9   n/a  (6.7)    5.2</p>
<p> secured on dwellings		    0.4   0.5  (0.5)    0.4</p>
<p>		  annualised 3mth	  5.4   5.4  (5.5)    4.2</p>
<p>    &quot;	 &quot;	  &quot;     yr/yr     5.1   5.0  (5.0)    4.0</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
